---
// About: who makes this and how. Written 2026-10-01 after Google's 09-28
// demotion, approved by Hidde in session ("moeten we niet open zijn dat we
// starten met officiele register en ai - maar dat we de gebruikers vragen om
// ons te helpen? en dat we contact opnemen met de lokale partijen?").
//
// Why it exists: Google's own self-assessment asks "Is it self-evident to your
// visitors who authored your content?" and "Is the use of automation,
// including AI-generation, self-evident to visitors through disclosures?", and
// this site answered neither anywhere. So it says plainly where the trees come
// from, that the stories are drafted with AI from the sources each tree page
// lists, and where readers and local organisations come in.
//
// Convention: AllTrails, komoot and iNaturalist all carry an About page linked
// from the footer.
//
// 2026-10-14: Hidde's own story, first name and photo on top, written by him
// ("ja ik denk dat het beter is dat ik deze pagina zelf schrijf"). The reason
// was trust, not ranking: a tree expert answered our mail that he could find
// nothing about who makes this. First name only, the project
// address info@ (not a personal one), no surname. The photo's EXIF was stripped
// (an iPhone file carries its GPS position). Layout after Dense Discovery's
// maker block: photo beside the text on desktop, above it on a phone. The four
// sections that narrated our process were cut on his "less is more"; the AI
// disclosure Google's self-assessment asks for stays as one sentence.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema, ldScript, SITE_SCHEMA, BASE_URL } from "../lib/schema";
import { submitLink } from "../lib/tree-copy";

const canonical = `${BASE_URL}/about`;
const crumbItems: [string, string | null][] = [["Home", BASE_URL], ["About", null]];
const description = "How Ancient Trees started with the old trees of Lisbon and Palermo, who makes it, and where its trees and stories come from.";

const graph = [
  ...SITE_SCHEMA,
  breadcrumbSchema(crumbItems, canonical),
  {
    "@type": "AboutPage",
    name: "About Ancient Trees",
    description,
    url: canonical,
  },
];
---
<Base title="About Ancient Trees" description={description} canonical={canonical} headExtra={ldScript(graph)}>
<main class="about">
  {/* Layout B (Hidde, 2026-10-14, after "make the pic a lot better"): the
      photograph as large as the text column and uncropped, held in view while
      the story scrolls (sticky), edge to edge above the story on a phone.
      Benchmarked against Polarsteps' full-bleed hero, which crops a portrait
      tree to a strip on desktop and loses the crown. */}
  <figure class="about-photo">
    <img src="/photos/about/hidde-cedar-1200.jpg" srcset="/photos/about/hidde-cedar-600.jpg 600w, /photos/about/hidde-cedar-1200.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) 100vw, 540px" width="1200" height="1600" alt="Hidde admiring a huge Japanese cedar in Kyushu">
    <figcaption>Me admiring a <a href="/taketa/cedars-of-noike-shrine">huge Japanese cedar in Kyushu</a></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="about-words">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbItems} />
    <h1>About Ancient Trees</h1>
    <p>The story of Ancient Trees actually started in Lisbon. I travelled there a lot for work, and when you travel for work you have some time to kill. Strolling through the many beautiful parks, I was fascinated by the old jacarandas and fig trees (not that I knew the species then). They seemed ages old, definitely planted by someone no longer living, for us to marvel at. When I later travelled to Palermo and accidentally parked in front of a huge old ficus, I was blown away, and I realised how much I enjoyed these encounters with ancient trees on my trips.</p>
    <p><strong class="about-mark">I'm not a tree expert, but I am a big fan.</strong> I hope to share this passion with others and make it easier for people to experience trees like these and simply enjoy them, the way I do.</p>
    <p>The site isn't perfect, and it needs your help to get better. You can <a href={submitLink("tree")}>add trees you like</a>, improve the current trees we have or add stories about trees to make it even more interesting to visit.</p>
    <p>If you really want to help, you can <a href="/cities">become the ambassador of your city</a> and help guide others to see remarkable trees in your city.</p>
    <p>The photo is me at a huge Japanese cedar I found recently, on our trip while testing the app. I work on the app every day to make it better. For questions, feedback or anything else, mail me at <a href="mailto:info@ancienttrees.app">info@ancienttrees.app</a>.</p>
    <p class="about-sign">Thanks,<br>Hidde</p>
    <div class="about-where">
      <h2>Where the trees come from</h2>
      <p>Most trees come from official registers of protected and monumental trees, the rest from tree societies, local newspapers and readers. The stories are written with AI and corrected by people who know the trees. All sources are on the <a href="/sources">sources page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
</Base>

<style>
  .about { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: calc(var(--header-h) + 2.25rem) 24px 4rem; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 56px; align-items: start; }
  .about-photo { margin: 0; position: sticky; top: calc(var(--header-h) + 24px); }
  .about-photo img { width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 3 / 4; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 18px; display: block; }
  .about-photo figcaption { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-mid); margin-top: 10px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .about-words h1 { font-size: 46px; line-height: 1.05; margin: 0 0 24px; }
  .about-words .about-sign { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .about-words p { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink-mid); font-weight: 300; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .about-mark { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 500; }
  .about-where { border-top: 1px solid var(--line, rgba(0, 0, 0, .08)); margin-top: 2.5rem; padding-top: 2rem; }
  .about-where h2 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  .about-where p { font-size: 15px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .about { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0; padding: var(--header-h) 0 3rem; }
    .about-photo { position: static; }
    .about-photo img { border-radius: 0; aspect-ratio: 4 / 5; }
    .about-photo figcaption { padding: 0 16px; }
    .about-words { padding: 24px 16px 0; }
    .about-words h1 { font-size: 36px; }
  }
</style>
